      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e49bb15506bf6a20ad07f197a4d422fe3916f7df9b2292aef2f3218ca38bb392",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Functional symmetry is converted into an amplitude-phase representation; a positive-shift boundary prescription and a selected critical-line cosine branch then produce indexed asymptotic and exact phase equations. Only a globally well-defined phase with exactly one solution for every index permits transfer from the critical-line count to saturation of the strip-wide count.",
